  "descriptionKey": "- A state-based conflict is defined by the [Uppsala Conflict Data Program (UCDP)](https://ucdp.uu.se/) as a conflict between two armed groups, at least one of which is a state, that causes at least 25 deaths during a year. This includes combatant and civilian deaths due to fighting.\n- A country is considered to participate in a conflict if they were a primary participant, which refers to those participants that have the main disagreement of the conflict.",
  "origins": [
